WEBVTT

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:04.380
<i>Behold, the vast world in which we live!</i>

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:09.910
<i>It is rampant with monsters 
that threaten human life.</i>

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:16.310
<i>This threat is opposed by 
countless adventurers! Heroes!</i>

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.180
<i>Every day, they face these 
dangerous battles...</i>

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:24.580
<i>To protect the people! To protect the world!</i>

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:31.340
And I, Alvin, am one of them!

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.200
Now in a party with Carla, the healer,

00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:38.700
my journey continues!

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:00.370
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:00.370
Don't Hurt Me,

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:00.370
My Healer!

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:14.530
<b>The first dungeon Alvin tackles with Carla is designed for...</b>

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:17.440
Alvin-san. Where are we going today?

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:18.420
A dungeon.

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:20.080
Be serious!

00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:21.850
I <i>am</i> serious!

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:24.020
What, you think I can't handle it?

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:27.260
I wasn't thinking that myself, 
but it might be the general consensus.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:28.840
Don't you worry!

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:32.170
I hear the place we're headed 
for is designed for beginners!

00:02:32.170 --> 00:02:34.540
In other words, it was built just for you.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:36.430
What, you think I'm the dungeon's owner?

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:38.770
Aha, I see.

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:40.130
You live there?

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:42.400
I told you, it's a dungeon!

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.810
Hey!

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:50.120
I found a building just ahead!

00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:51.810
That must be the place!

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:54.890
At last, my first dungeon!

00:02:55.640 --> 00:02:57.570
It does set the heart racing.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.020
Okay, let's go!

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:07.080
<b>Welcome SUPER Beginners Only
Dungeon</b>

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.080
<b>Safety Guaranteed</b>

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:14.480
This is a unique house you live in.

00:03:14.480 --> 00:03:16.220
Did you have it designed?

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:18.020
It's <i>not</i> my house!

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:21.670
If it was, I would curse 
the designer for eternity!

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:23.170
What should we do?

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:25.480
It's not exactly what I 
was expecting, but...

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:26.980
I guess we should go in—

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:28.350
Halt!

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:31.570
A monster?!

00:03:33.590 --> 00:03:36.440
Lower your sword, warrior.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:38.480
I have no desire to fight!

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.270
Wh-What?!

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:43.150
Maybe you don't, but we do!

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:44.420
Let's do this!

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:47.000
What kind of bloodthirsty 
holy woman are you?!

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.660
Do you mean to enter this dungeon?

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:51.190
What if we do?

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:52.130
Are you going to try to stop us?

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:55.240
As I said before, I have no desire to fight.

00:03:55.560 --> 00:03:58.140
See? He said he wants to fight!

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:58.260
But this is a dungeon for extreme beginners.

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.880
No, you're the one who's 
been trying to fight!

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.880
I must determine if you are worthy to—

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.380
Hey! Are you listening?!

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:04.890
Listening to what?

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:07.270
I knew it. You weren't listening...

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:10.760
And I was trying so hard to 
sound cool and impressive!

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:16.190
You were saying that only beginners 
can enter this dungeon, right?

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:19.180
Thank goodness, one of them has sense...

00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:20.420
No need to worry there.

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:23.340
Alvin-san has an annual 
pass to beginnership.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:23.950
Do not!

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.280
Very well.

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.480
I will investigate, and confirm your words.

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.210
Let us begin!

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:39.820
This is...

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.630
Wha?! A h-h-hundred?!

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:49.630
Beginner level 100?!

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:51.510
That's nuts, man!

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:53.560
I had a feeling this would happen!

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:56.380
Patheticness level 100?

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.020
I can see it.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.900
I don't think he said <i>that</i>!

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:05.040
W-Well, they say it's not good to 
stray too far from your roots...

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:05.490
Pfft

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.370
You're just making it worse.

00:05:09.730 --> 00:05:11.670
Enter away!

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:14.790
There's a song playing!

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:17.050
At last, our first dungeon!

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:19.430
Time to beat it!

00:05:19.430 --> 00:05:20.290
Yeah.

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:22.390
Take care!

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:24.040
We will, thanks!

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:27.030
I'm exhausted.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:29.200
We're just a few steps in, 
and I'm already exhausted.

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:32.140
<i>Regardless, this is still a dungeon!</i>

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:34.960
<i>I need to remain on my guard!</i>

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:38.810
You never know what kind 
of traps might await!

00:05:38.810 --> 00:05:40.290
Listen up, party!

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:43.490
This may be for beginners, 
but it's still a dungeon!

00:05:43.490 --> 00:05:45.770
You have to keep a close eye 
on everything around—

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:47.770
Behold!

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:51.780
Alvin-san's patented 
patheticness-level-100 specialty!

00:06:01.510 --> 00:06:04.300
Alvin-san? Are you all right?

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:08.720
There's a cushion at the bottom,

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:11.100
and a ladder on the wall.

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:14.590
Just what you'd expect from 
a beginners' dungeon trap.

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:19.020
You should really climb up already.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.470
I don't think you're actually hurt.

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:37.890
He seems pretty down.

00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:40.870
Good grief. We'll have to reassure him.

00:06:42.190 --> 00:06:43.510
Alvin-san.

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:48.110
That was a magnificent hole-in-one!

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:49.190
Practically professional!

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:50.770
A perfect example of what not to do!

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:53.280
That's not the way you reassure someone!

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:55.300
And it's not like I sprung 
the trap on purpose!

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.560
Yes, yes. I know.

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:01.680
In fact, I prepared a magic item to 
deal with traps just like these.

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:02.700
Here. Take it.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:04.380
What, really?

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:05.740
What the heck...

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:07.950
If you had one of those, 
why didn't you say—

00:07:07.950 --> 00:07:08.390
Wait.

00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:11.570
What's this thing?

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.170
An ordinary cloth?

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:16.160
Good grief. You amateurs 
don't know anything.

00:07:16.570 --> 00:07:17.710
Listen to me.

00:07:17.710 --> 00:07:19.760
The next time you trigger a trap...

00:07:20.120 --> 00:07:22.060
The next time I trigger a trap...?

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:24.410
It'll probably be very embarrassing,

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:26.500
so you can use that to wipe away your tears!

00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:28.810
So it's just a handkerchief!

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:30.270
And I'm not crying!

00:07:30.270 --> 00:07:31.380
What a rude thing to say!

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:33.970
It's actually a very useful cleaning aid!

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:35.260
So it's just a rag!

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:37.630
I just have to not spring 
any more traps, right?

00:07:37.630 --> 00:07:38.230
Come on!

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:42.810
Stay alert, keep a close 
eye on your surroundings.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:45.240
Detect dangers early, and avoid them.

00:07:45.240 --> 00:07:48.320
Stay alert, keep a close eye 
on your surroundings...

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.690
Does it seem like it's 
getting darker to you?

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:52.280
It is getting dark.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:54.280
Be sure to watch your step.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:55.610
I will.

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:57.270
Alvin-san.

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:00.630
Do you think that lever 
might turn on the lights?

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:03.670
That lever?

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:06.320
Hey, you might be right!

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:09.200
It's hard to see traps when 
it's this dark, after all!

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.330
Just what I'd expect from 
a beginners' dungeon!

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:27.810
I'm not crying!

00:08:27.810 --> 00:08:29.630
Come on! Be vulnerable!

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:32.450
Get that rag away for me, you little...

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:37.180
C'mon. Stop playing around, 
and let's get going!

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:38.590
We're not playing around!

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:43.100
Stay alert, keep a close 
eye on your surroundings.

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:44.700
By the way, Alvin...

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:46.240
Detect dangers early, and avoid them.

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:48.460
That was a pretty sad trap 
you triggered back there...

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:51.520
You think you're not cut out 
for this adventurer thing?

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:52.920
Not cut out

00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:55.490
You've got it all wrong.

00:08:55.490 --> 00:08:56.170
I do?

00:08:56.680 --> 00:09:00.080
Alvin-san is triggering 
the traps intentionally

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:02.690
so that we don't accidentally 
spring them ourselves!

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:05.680
What? Really?!

00:09:05.680 --> 00:09:07.470
Of course.

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:11.000
He'd never fall for such 
a silly trap, normally.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.750
Right, Alvin-san?

00:09:14.250 --> 00:09:16.510
Was it that obvious?

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:18.160
I knew it!

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:21.900
Well... the duty of a warrior is 
to shield his comrades from harm.

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:24.560
You're a true paragon, Alvin-san!

00:09:24.560 --> 00:09:26.570
H-Hey, cut it out...

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:31.450
But you could have just warned us.

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:34.170
Why put yourself through that on purpose?

00:09:34.170 --> 00:09:36.390
Don't build me up just to tear me back down!

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:40.680
Is triggering traps your thing 
these days or something?

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.220
Don't make it sound like a hobby!

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:45.480
Hey, Alvin, look down!

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:46.150
What?

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:52.930
Damn! We're locked in!

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:56.940
The walls!

00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:58.100
Not good!

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.200
They're going to crush us!

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:05.280
What do we do?!

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:15.130
Looks like we can just hold them back.

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:19.880
Alvin-san. Alvin-san!

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:24.640
How'd you get out there? 
Did you use a spell?

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:28.710
No, there's a door in the bars.

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:29.450
See?

00:10:30.620 --> 00:10:34.900
When you panic, it's easy to 
miss the forest for the trees.

00:10:39.940 --> 00:10:43.870
Stay alert, keep a close eye 
on your surroundings...

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:44.940
Isn't this nice, Alvin-san?

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:52.170
I'll bet the traps are so happy 
that you're springing them all!

00:10:52.170 --> 00:10:54.180
Don't anthropomorphize the traps!

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:57.000
Traps exist to be sprung!

00:10:57.000 --> 00:11:01.050
From their point of view, 
you're the ideal adventurer!

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:03.670
I don't want to be the traps' ideal!

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:06.100
Hey, look over there!

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:09.120
Is that...

00:11:17.010 --> 00:11:18.590
It's a door, right?

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:21.320
I don't see any other way to go...

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:24.130
Was this whole thing one straight line?

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:30.330
Please Ring
↑     Bell

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:30.320
There's something like a button here.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:33.900
I'll bet it's another trap.

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:36.060
It's pretty clearly dicey...

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:38.300
The law of odds does suggest it's trap.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:39.980
Right?

00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:41.760
What do we do?

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:47.530
Go right ahead, professional Alvin!

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:48.540
I'm not a professional!

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:50.180
Do your usual thing!

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:52.060
This is <i>not</i> my usual thing!

00:11:54.440 --> 00:11:57.600
But if you insist, I'll press it!

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:03.030
<b>S
o

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:03.030
<b>S
o

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:03.030
<b>S
o

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:03.030
<b>S
o

00:11:58.030 --> 00:12:03.030
<b>S
o

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:05.990
Please Ring
↑     Bell

00:12:03.440 --> 00:12:07.280
Stay alert, keep a close 
eye on your surroundings.

00:12:07.280 --> 00:12:10.010
Detect dangers early, and avoid them.

00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:12.150
All right. I'll press it!

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:12.910
Right...

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:15.310
It's a total trap, man.

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:16.630
It's not safe!

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.940
But there's no other way to proceed.

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:20.680
I know, but...

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:22.810
I'm pushing it. I'm pushing it.

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:26.050
I'm pushing it! I really am!

00:12:26.050 --> 00:12:28.480
Don't panic if something goes wrong!

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.450
But where's the trap going to come from?

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:31.740
From above? From below?

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:33.200
From the right? From the left?

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:34.710
Even from behind?!

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:35.800
Come on, you guys!

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:40.250
But... we don't know that pressing this 
button will necessarily open the door.

00:12:40.250 --> 00:12:42.230
I'm just so worried that it's a trap.

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:45.130
Perhaps I should proceed cautiously...

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:48.810
I know! Pressing the button with my 
sword should make it a bit safer!

00:12:49.290 --> 00:12:51.740
This should keep me out 
of range of the trap!

00:12:51.740 --> 00:12:53.230
Okay! Here I go!

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:54.240
Hey!

00:13:02.160 --> 00:13:03.460
It's open.

00:13:03.460 --> 00:13:05.260
You just broke it down!

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:07.320
And don't give me that ugly little wink!

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:09.260
Well, it turned out same way.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:11.630
If you ignore the property damage, sure!

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:14.310
Hey! What was that sound?

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:19.580
It sounded like someone breaking 
through a door with a tieshankao!

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:21.950
What's going on here?

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:24.820
<b>Domestic</b>

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:24.810
The door really is broken!

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:26.330
Something's here!

00:13:26.640 --> 00:13:28.290
I-Intruder!

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:30.690
I think <i>we're</i> the intruders here...

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:33.280
Are you guys... adventurers?

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:34.450
Well... yeah.

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:36.450
I knew it!

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:39.140
Well, don't just stand around all day!

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:40.010
Come on in!

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:44.170
Hey... he's acting like the welcome wagon.

00:13:44.170 --> 00:13:45.410
Could this be a trap, too?

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.560
Let's just play along for now.

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:51.270
Even if it's a trap, it's designed for 
beginners, so anyone who fell for it would...

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:53.330
Whoops.

00:13:53.330 --> 00:13:54.090
Hey.

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:57.140
Come on in! Don't be shy!

00:13:57.140 --> 00:13:59.050
Out with it already!

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:00.290
I'd rather not.

00:14:00.290 --> 00:14:02.380
Come on! Right this way!

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:12.130
Go on! Have yourselves a seat!

00:14:12.130 --> 00:14:13.330
R-Right...

00:14:19.200 --> 00:14:20.540
It's not much, but...

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.010
O-Of course. Thank you.

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:26.250
<i>Could it be... poison?!</i>

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.430
<i>She already drank it!</i>

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:30.740
It's cold! And super gross!

00:14:30.740 --> 00:14:32.010
Don't just say that!

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:34.360
I-I'm sorry!

00:14:34.360 --> 00:14:37.040
I'll brew up a new batch right away!

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.600
<b>Cow</b>

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.600
Hospitality

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.600
Fashion

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:40.600
Weight

00:14:37.800 --> 00:14:40.350
He's way too hospitable!

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:43.490
Anyway, who exactly are you?

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:45.660
Snort!

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:48.130
I am this dungeon's master!

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:52.220
You've strayed too far into 
my lair, foolish adventurer!

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:56.410
I think it's a bit late for that.

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:58.490
And you should probably 
find a better outfit.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:14:59.500
<b>Domestic</b>

00:14:59.500 --> 00:15:01.670
Well, even if you are a beginner,

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:05.100
nobody would ever spring those 
ridiculously basic traps...

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:09.900
Hang on a minute.

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:12.070
Did you spring the traps?

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:12.920
Ack.

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:17.650
That's hilarious!

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:21.320
I can't believe an adventurer fell 
for those lame, little traps!

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:24.010
Even for a beginner, that's just...

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:27.680
What's so funny about that?

00:15:27.980 --> 00:15:30.410
We lost people to those traps!

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:32.660
Could you please not make 
it sound like I died?

00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:34.840
I-It can't be...

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:40.850
My perfect safety record... shattered!

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:41.910
Hey! I'm alive!

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:46.160
What have I done?!

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:49.700
At least you recognize the 
wrongness of your actions.

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:52.790
I didn't mean to kill anybody!

00:15:52.790 --> 00:15:56.270
Moo!

00:15:54.830 --> 00:15:58.220
You're a monster! At least, 
have the guts to kill someone!

00:15:58.500 --> 00:16:00.640
Everyone makes mistakes.

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:04.350
What's important is finding a way to atone.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:06.550
You can find that way now.

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:08.230
Are you shaking him down, holy woman?

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:10.160
I understand.

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:12.180
Wait just a moment.

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:16.000
Although I'm afraid... this is all I have.

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:18.720
Business has been so bad...

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:20.440
Well, better than nothing.

00:16:23.780 --> 00:16:25.760
A coin pendant?

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:27.490
A magic item?!

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:31.920
No, it's a souvenir we give out to visitors.

00:16:32.660 --> 00:16:35.750
It looks just like an 
ordinary pendant to me.

00:16:35.750 --> 00:16:36.700
But what if...

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:37.430
What is it?

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:39.680
It's garbage! Completely undesirable!

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:41.680
At least <i>try</i> to be nice!

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:51.930
Well, does everyone have their drink?

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:50.940
M
V
P

00:16:52.400 --> 00:16:58.320
Then, a toast to the Carla Party's 
conquest of the dungeon!

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.820
Cheers!

00:17:01.090 --> 00:17:04.230
Great work today, everyone!

00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:07.220
Hang on a minute!

00:17:07.220 --> 00:17:08.600
This can't be right!

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:11.610
Why are we having a friendly 
drink with monsters?

00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:14.580
And why didn't I get a drink of my own?!

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:17.550
And this seems like a good time to ask...

00:17:17.550 --> 00:17:20.230
Exactly how long are you 
going to tag along with us?

00:17:20.230 --> 00:17:23.710
And if you're the dungeon's master, 
shouldn't you, at least, try to be scary?

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:25.440
I'll serve the salad.

00:17:25.440 --> 00:17:27.610
This is no time to be serving salad!

00:17:27.610 --> 00:17:30.150
Let's let our hair down.

00:17:30.150 --> 00:17:32.490
Alvin-san, would you 
please rub my shoulders?

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:33.890
You're a tyrant!

00:17:33.890 --> 00:17:35.380
Alvin-san.

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:36.610
What now?!

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:37.860
You've gotten too excited.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:39.000
It's not knights.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:40.510
I'm <i>angry</i>!

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:42.860
And you're the one who's too excited!

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:45.070
What's with that outfit? 
Is it your birthday?

00:17:46.280 --> 00:17:49.790
I think you're the one with the 
strange outfit, Alvin-san.

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:51.830
Did you think this was a 
warrior costume party?

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:53.990
It's my usual outfit!

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:58.360
But I understand why you're so excited.

00:17:58.360 --> 00:18:01.840
This is my first dungeon 
clear as an adventurer, too.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:04.470
It's your first, too?

00:18:04.840 --> 00:18:05.850
Yes.

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:09.090
It's not cold!

00:18:09.090 --> 00:18:11.040
<i>I see now.</i>

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:12.390
<i>Given her personality and all,</i>

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:15.190
<i>she probably gets kicked out 
of any party she joins.</i>

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:18.360
<i>Maybe that's why she's indulging 
in that silly outfit.</i>

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:23.110
<i>I've been turned down from various parties 
for not being good enough, myself.</i>

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:25.680
Excuse me! Do you think I could join—

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:28.110
Sorry. I need a little higher level...

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:30.580
Look at that! A veteran rookie!

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:33.310
Sounds like...

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:38.110
You two beating your first dungeon 
is an event worth celebrating.

00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:39.520
A red-letter day!

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:43.400
Well, I'm not sure I'd say 
we <i>beat</i> it, exactly...

00:18:43.400 --> 00:18:44.490
A red-letter day...

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:50.020
A red-letter day for our party.

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:53.400
What is this? Are you happy?

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:55.790
No, I feel perfectly normal!

00:18:56.660 --> 00:18:59.580
Did I nail it? Are you blushing?!

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:04.950
You got a problem? I'll send you to hell!

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:07.480
<i>She's dangerous, even when she's blushing.</i>

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:10.720
Well, since we both did something 
worth celebrating...

00:19:10.720 --> 00:19:11.450
Here.

00:19:12.030 --> 00:19:13.310
What is it?

00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:14.710
You don't know what it means?

00:19:14.710 --> 00:19:15.830
It's a high five.

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:18.930
When a party accomplishes 
something together,

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:20.220
it's just what they do.

00:19:20.820 --> 00:19:23.220
When a party accomplishes something...

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:25.210
Yeah, big doubts!

00:19:26.160 --> 00:19:29.050
Your assertion that you 
know things parties do

00:19:29.050 --> 00:19:32.180
contradicts your earlier statement 
that you've never been in a party.

00:19:32.180 --> 00:19:32.990
It's fishy!

00:19:32.990 --> 00:19:34.610
It's not fishy!

00:19:34.610 --> 00:19:36.250
I think your true objective is...

00:19:36.800 --> 00:19:40.110
to use a high five as an excuse to touch me!

00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:42.030
Yeah, yeah.

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:44.490
I'm okay with not doing 
it if you don't want to.

00:19:47.970 --> 00:19:51.370
Well, we are a party, after all.

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:54.530
I suppose I can allow you one little touch.

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:57.040
<i>This girl is a serious pain in my ass.</i>

00:19:57.510 --> 00:19:59.160
Okay, fine.

00:19:59.160 --> 00:19:59.890
Here.

00:20:00.120 --> 00:20:02.650
I-If you insist...

00:20:03.140 --> 00:20:06.710
Then, to our first dungeon clear...

00:20:06.710 --> 00:20:08.880
<i>Good grief. Sheesh.</i>

00:20:08.880 --> 00:20:10.770
<i>She's over the moon!</i>

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:12.900
Well done!

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:22.410
Thank you for clearing our dungeon!

00:20:22.410 --> 00:20:24.320
Thanks for coming!

00:20:24.320 --> 00:20:26.330
The food was so good!

00:20:26.330 --> 00:20:27.830
We loved it!

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.620
It's been a blast!

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:31.320
Have a good day!

00:20:33.460 --> 00:20:35.430
What an entertaining party.

00:20:35.430 --> 00:20:38.100
I'd better get on fixing that door.

00:20:38.860 --> 00:20:42.260
How long are you gonna wear that getup?

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:44.410
Cow-san gave it to me for the occasion.

00:20:44.410 --> 00:20:47.540
It would be rude to remove 
it while he's watching.

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:49.120
You care about rudeness?

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:49.970
Yes.

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:53.240
By the way, Alvin...

00:20:53.240 --> 00:20:54.500
What is it?

00:20:54.500 --> 00:20:57.820
He told me that button in 
the dungeon wasn't a trap.

00:20:57.820 --> 00:20:59.770
It was just a doorbell.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.260
Was it?

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:03.400
Makes sense, for a beginner's dungeon...

00:21:04.520 --> 00:21:06.520
Well, it's getting late.

00:21:06.520 --> 00:21:09.030
I'd like to reach an inn 
before it gets dark.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:10.270
Right, Carla?

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:13.290
Wh-Wh-What are you talking about?

00:21:13.290 --> 00:21:15.120
I was saying, we could get to an inn...

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:15.910
Yes, of course, an inn!

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:17.080
Yes, let us proceed!

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:19.210
Excuse me. Carla-san?

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:20.450
You're acting weird.

00:21:20.450 --> 00:21:21.790
W-Weird?

00:21:21.790 --> 00:21:24.470
I don't like being called 
strange by funny-types.

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:26.700
Do you mean funny as in amusing?

00:21:26.700 --> 00:21:28.230
Or deviant?

00:21:28.230 --> 00:21:29.160
Deviant.

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:30.730
What?!

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:35.210
Eh? Kinoko-san is gone.

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:36.170
Really?

00:21:36.170 --> 00:21:37.960
Well, he'll catch up soon enough.

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:39.180
I'm sure he will.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:42.570
And that spares us paying for his room.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:44.590
You're one stone-hearted holy woman.

00:21:44.590 --> 00:21:47.320
I'm just worried about 
your wallet, Alvin-san.

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:49.330
Why do you assume I'm poor?!

00:21:50.030 --> 00:21:55.040
<b>Where am I?</b>

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:25.560 --> 00:23:27.300
Next episode's title is...

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:29.770
"The owner of the inn they 
visit seems very nice,

00:23:29.770 --> 00:23:33.650
but Carla accidentally forces him 
to reveal a surprising true form

00:23:33.650 --> 00:23:35.090
and then an old lady 
they happen to meet

00:23:35.090 --> 00:23:36.720
on the road also reveals 
an unexpected side

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:38.490
and this confirms once again that..."

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>See you then!</b>

00:23:37.050 --> 00:23:40.130
<b>"The owner of the inn they visit seems very nice,
but Carla accidentally forces him to reveal a surprising true
form and then an old lady they happen to meet on the road
also reveals an unexpected side and this confirms
once again that there are monsters in this world that
disguise themselves as humans but by the way the
name of the inn is "Stay! Burin" and some of you might not
know where that name comes from but it's from a pretty
famous show so if you know it you're definitely wallowing
in nostalgia right now and that's the deal with episode 5."</b>

00:23:38.490 --> 00:23:40.490
Is it possible for anyone to say all this?
